  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 5.01,
      "end": 11.01,
      "text": "On 275 and 285. Also in stereo on VHF. This is National Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.71,
      "end": 28.75,
      "text": "This is Thomas the Clown here, TV on the radio and welcome once again to the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.63,
      "end": 34.27,
      "text": "And this evening out of the archives from the 60s we feature one of the first and the last session",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.27,
      "end": 38.91,
      "text": "ever recorded for the BBC by the Yardbirds. They feature Eric Clapton and Jimmy Page.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.91,
      "end": 56.9,
      "text": "Also a repeat of our ace session by Taurus. And we got classic cuts from Black Oak Arkansas,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.9,
      "end": 59.3,
      "text": "ZZ Top, ACDC and Boston, among others,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.38,
      "end": 62.42,
      "text": "and new releases by Samson, Judas Priest, Michael Schenker,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.6,
      "end": 64.34,
      "text": "Tigers of Pan tang and Diamondhead.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.82,
      "end": 69.4,
      "text": "And a track from Drama, the new LP by Yes, the brand new line-up.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.82,
      "end": 72.66,
      "text": "But this evening, we start with a classic by Mountain.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 815.01,
      "end": 817.91,
      "text": "Well, I bet you money if you haven't got that album, you don't know who that is.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 819.19,
      "end": 823.15,
      "text": "That was Samson, and it's a track from their new album, which is out on Gem Records.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 823.25,
      "end": 826.65,
      "text": "The album's called Head On, and the track you heard was Walking Out On You.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 826.65,
      "end": 834.48,
      "text": "And before that, Mountain, a real classic from Yonks Ago, Nantucket's sleigh ride to Owen Coffin.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 835.18,
      "end": 837.58,
      "text": "And that was played specially for Pete and Bartley from Swansea.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 838.2,
      "end": 841.56,
      "text": "And also for Robert Ingham, a.k.a. Big Bad Bob.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 841.66,
      "end": 845.3,
      "text": "He lives in Grimsby and he wants me to say hello to the infamous Stella of Howell.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 846.16,
      "end": 850.72,
      "text": "And also we played that track by Mountain for Andrew Harding, who lives in Hainault in Essex.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 854.07,
      "end": 858.61,
      "text": "10.14 on the Friday Rock Show, here's the first of four from our repeat session by Taurus.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 858.61,
      "end": 892.81,
      "text": "The record got a terrible slating on Roundtable, I don't really know why, because I think it's one of the best records they've ever made, and ultimately it's going to become their anthem, wherever they appear live, I would imagine, everybody's going to know the words, they'll stand up and they'll sway and they'll sing it, united.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 892.81,
      "end": 1075.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 892.81,
      "end": 1075.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1080.0,
      "end": 1290.55,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1080.0,
      "end": 1290.55,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1290.55,
      "end": 1293.5,
      "text": "10.21 on the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1293.56,
      "end": 1295.9,
      "text": "A nice bit of criticism about a record we played last week.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1296.0,
      "end": 1298.04,
      "text": "It comes from Stephen Ainslie of Chelmsford.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1298.1,
      "end": 1299.56,
      "text": "He just wrote P.S. on his letter.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1300.06,
      "end": 1303.72,
      "text": "Holocaust Heavy Metal Mania kept me amused for the rest of the show last night.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1304.1,
      "end": 1305.88,
      "text": "Will you have the Baron Knights on next week?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1306.26,
      "end": 1308.6,
      "text": "If they do a heavy metal send-up, maybe we will one day.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1309.3,
      "end": 1312.12,
      "text": "Also I'd like to mention a lady who's too shy to have her name mentioned.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1312.26,
      "end": 1313.78,
      "text": "Her name is N. Onimus.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1314.2,
      "end": 1317.12,
      "text": "And I'd like to say a very good evening to another lady who's very shy.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1317.22,
      "end": 1318.9,
      "text": "But I do know her name. Her name is Helen.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1322.84,
      "end": 1325.22,
      "text": "And here's a little-known track by Black Oak, Arkansas.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1325.78,
      "end": 1332.38,
      "text": "On their one and only performance in this country last year,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1620.0,
      "end": 1712.26,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1620.0,
      "end": 1712.26,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1712.26,
      "end": 1715.12,
      "text": "And also, in the Girl's School set, they do it twice.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1715.28,
      "end": 1719.28,
      "text": "At least Tony Wilson said they did it twice when he was watching them on stage at Folkestone.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1719.4,
      "end": 1721.46,
      "text": "I think he's in love with a lead guitarist, but that's another story.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1721.98,
      "end": 1727.26,
      "text": "And Girl's School are finishing their current tour at the Civic Hall in St Albans tomorrow night.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1727.44,
      "end": 1730.88,
      "text": "And another band is supporting them, who've been on this show, a band by the name of More.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1731.16,
      "end": 1734.88,
      "text": "Prior to that, you heard Black Oak, Arkansas, and a track from Balls of Fire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1735.0,
      "end": 1737.82,
      "text": "The track was rock and roll, and that was for Gary and YAT",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1737.82,
      "end": 1741.64,
      "text": "and all the Hieronymus Bosch fans worldwide.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1741.64,
      "end": 1743.77,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1741.64,
      "end": 1743.77,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1748.77,
      "end": 1751.97,
      "text": "1029, back to 1965 and the Yardbirds.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1751.97,
      "end": 1983.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1751.97,
      "end": 2301.12,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1983.73,
      "end": 2005.3,
      "text": "And here's the first number on the show by that great group, the Yardbirds.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2005.92,
      "end": 2016.12,
      "text": "The Yardbirds had an archive session that featured the work of Mr. Eric Clapton on lead guitar.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2301.12,
      "end": 2302.56,
      "text": "And these are the tracks that we played for you.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2302.66,
      "end": 2307.1,
      "text": "First was For Your Love, then I'm Not Talking, then I Wish You Would, and then Heart Full of Soul.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2307.74,
      "end": 2314.97,
      "text": "And we got another session by the Yardbirds coming up later on in the program that features Mr. Jimmy Page.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2319.96,
      "end": 2321.6,
      "text": "And now here's a track by ACDC.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2321.6,
      "end": 2323.98,
      "text": "was recorded on an album called TNT",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2323.98,
      "end": 2326.42,
      "text": "that came out in Australia way back in 1975,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2326.72,
      "end": 2328.54,
      "text": "and I don't think this track has been included",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2328.54,
      "end": 2330.34,
      "text": "on any other album that's been released.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2330.88,
      "end": 2332.88,
      "text": "In other words, I don't think it's been put out in this country.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2333.0,
      "end": 2333.94,
      "text": "It's called Rocker.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2340.0,
      "end": 2515.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2340.0,
      "end": 2515.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2520.0,
      "end": 2810.51,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2520.0,
      "end": 2810.51,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2810.51,
      "end": 2813.63,
      "text": "ACDC, from the album that jumped right in at number one this week",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2813.63,
      "end": 2816.13,
      "text": "in the top 30 album chart, the album called Back in Black.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2816.23,
      "end": 2817.47,
      "text": "The track was Harold's Bells.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2817.93,
      "end": 2820.01,
      "text": "And before that, something from an Australian import,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2820.25,
      "end": 2824.07,
      "text": "the album called TNT that came out in 1975 featuring ACDC.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2824.25,
      "end": 2825.55,
      "text": "That track was called Rocker.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2825.55,
      "end": 2829.15,
      "text": "And incidentally, you can get both of those Australian imports,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2829.27,
      "end": 2832.29,
      "text": "that's the Australian version of High Voltage and TNT,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2832.51,
      "end": 2834.21,
      "text": "through Pacific Records in London.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2835.45,
      "end": 2837.71,
      "text": "Play that whole ACDC set for everybody",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2837.71,
      "end": 2841.01,
      "text": "who's going to join the sixth form at Ashington High",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2841.01,
      "end": 2842.03,
      "text": "up there in Northumberland.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2842.19,
      "end": 2843.53,
      "text": "Best wishes from Ashby Davidson.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2844.13,
      "end": 2847.09,
      "text": "And also for a gentleman by the name of Alastair Gibson",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2847.09,
      "end": 2849.57,
      "text": "who lives in Eatonwick near Windsor in Berkshire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2849.67,
      "end": 2850.97,
      "text": "Nice part of the world, that is.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2851.79,
      "end": 2854.11,
      "text": "And for Mick Parker and Steve Brindle and Dave Knott",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2854.11,
      "end": 2856.29,
      "text": "and any of the Harwood heavies who may be listening,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2856.35,
      "end": 2862.75,
      "text": "up there in bolton lots of best wishes from phil finch and also for donald stark who lives in",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2862.75,
      "end": 2867.53,
      "text": "glasgow and finally for everybody going into the fifth year at people's high i didn't know",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2867.53,
      "end": 2871.83,
      "text": "andy was into the school business that's pin and mike and angus and hardy best wishes from",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2871.83,
      "end": 2881.43,
      "text": "andrew connor here's taurus and you know how i'm feeling the album's coming out because there's",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3240.0,
      "end": 3402.01,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3240.0,
      "end": 3402.01,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3402.01,
      "end": 3406.53,
      "text": "no release date on the white label that we're playing it playing it from rather the album is",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3406.53,
      "end": 3407.77,
      "text": "by Michael Schenker",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3407.77,
      "end": 3408.91,
      "text": "and that track",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3408.91,
      "end": 3409.49,
      "text": "you heard there",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3409.49,
      "end": 3409.95,
      "text": "was called",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3409.95,
      "end": 3410.69,
      "text": "Cry for the Nation",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3410.69,
      "end": 3411.85,
      "text": "and it's coming out",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3411.85,
      "end": 3413.25,
      "text": "shortly on Chrysalis",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3413.25,
      "end": 3416.23,
      "text": "and before that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3416.23,
      "end": 3417.21,
      "text": "you heard Taurus",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3417.21,
      "end": 3418.29,
      "text": "and the track called",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3418.29,
      "end": 3419.27,
      "text": "You Know How I'm Feeling",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3419.27,
      "end": 3421.58,
      "text": "3 minutes to 11",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3421.58,
      "end": 3422.28,
      "text": "it's time for the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3422.28,
      "end": 3423.14,
      "text": "Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3423.14,
      "end": 3423.5,
      "text": "right",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3423.5,
      "end": 3424.4,
      "text": "the tracks we played",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3424.4,
      "end": 3424.9,
      "text": "you last week",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3424.9,
      "end": 3425.38,
      "text": "were these",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3425.38,
      "end": 3426.66,
      "text": "Parallels",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3426.66,
      "end": 3427.38,
      "text": "by Yes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3427.38,
      "end": 3428.83,
      "text": "from Going for the One",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3428.83,
      "end": 3430.03,
      "text": "recorded in Montreux",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3430.03,
      "end": 3430.63,
      "text": "in Switzerland",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3430.63,
      "end": 3432.03,
      "text": "Smoke on the Water",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3432.03,
      "end": 3432.89,
      "text": "by Deep Purple",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3432.89,
      "end": 3433.91,
      "text": "with reference to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3433.91,
      "end": 3434.95,
      "text": "We All Came Out",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3434.95,
      "end": 3435.55,
      "text": "to Montreux",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3435.55,
      "end": 3437.25,
      "text": "and also to Swiss Time",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3437.25,
      "end": 3438.79,
      "text": "and then Heat Strokes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3438.79,
      "end": 3439.45,
      "text": "by Krokus",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3439.45,
      "end": 3440.45,
      "text": "from Metal Rendezvous,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3440.91,
      "end": 3442.83,
      "text": "Krokus being a Swiss-based band.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3443.79,
      "end": 3444.85,
      "text": "And a Maltese lead singer.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3446.64,
      "end": 3447.9,
      "text": "Loads of people wrote in,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3448.0,
      "end": 3449.26,
      "text": "and thanks to all of you who did.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3449.5,
      "end": 3450.38,
      "text": "Every letter was read,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3450.42,
      "end": 3451.66,
      "text": "I promise you that, this afternoon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3451.98,
      "end": 3453.66,
      "text": "But as usual, there can only be one winner",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3453.66,
      "end": 3455.46,
      "text": "because we're running short of money around here.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3456.08,
      "end": 3457.64,
      "text": "And the winner this week is Dave Bailey",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3457.64,
      "end": 3459.5,
      "text": "of number two, Ringgold's Way,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3459.76,
      "end": 3460.84,
      "text": "Street in Somerset.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3460.96,
      "end": 3461.86,
      "text": "Dave, congratulations.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3462.12,
      "end": 3463.66,
      "text": "You get yourself a £10 record token.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3464.44,
      "end": 3471.28,
      "text": "Our compliments.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3471.66,
      "end": 3473.34,
      "text": "And now, with our compliments,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3473.58,
      "end": 3474.84,
      "text": "here's the Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3474.84,
      "end": 3476.22,
      "text": "put together by Dave Bailey.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3476.58,
      "end": 3480.92,
      "text": "Three bits of music, and there certainly is a theme somewhere in them.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3481.2,
      "end": 3487.2,
      "text": "Street and Somerset, a nice selection and a clever idea.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3487.2,
      "end": 4208.8,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3487.2,
      "end": 4208.8,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4208.8,
      "end": 4211.04,
      "text": "If you think you know what the Friday Night Connection is,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4211.1,
      "end": 4214.1,
      "text": "if it has crept into your imagination,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4216.36,
      "end": 4219.66,
      "text": "then put down the answer on a postcard or in a letter",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4219.66,
      "end": 4222.08,
      "text": "or any form of communication you like and send it to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4222.08,
      "end": 4223.58,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4223.58,
      "end": 4229.44,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1, London, W1A 4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4229.44,
      "end": 4233.93,
      "text": "You win the Friday Night Connection, you get a £10 record token.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4238.57,
      "end": 4247.46,
      "text": "Ten minutes after eleven is our time here on the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4247.56,
      "end": 4250.18,
      "text": "And I announced on this programme some many weeks ago now",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4250.18,
      "end": 4253.56,
      "text": "that John Anderson and Rick Wakeman had left Yes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4253.56,
      "end": 4257.24,
      "text": "and the Buggles were going to join up with the remainder of Yes.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4257.76,
      "end": 4259.32,
      "text": "There was a heck of a reaction.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4259.56,
      "end": 4261.92,
      "text": "Now, I know pretty well that the reaction was,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4262.04,
      "end": 4264.7,
      "text": "you're joking, it's not going to work.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4265.16,
      "end": 4266.86,
      "text": "Well, now you can make your mind up",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4266.86,
      "end": 4268.86,
      "text": "because here's a track from their forthcoming album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4268.88,
      "end": 4271.88,
      "text": "It comes out on the 22nd of this month",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4271.88,
      "end": 4273.16,
      "text": "Have a listen to this",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4273.16,
      "end": 4275.8,
      "text": "It's magical and it's called Into The Lens",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4275.8,
      "end": 4282.4,
      "text": "That's from the forthcoming album by the new line-up of Yes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4320.0,
      "end": 4789.21,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4320.0,
      "end": 4789.21,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4789.21,
      "end": 4791.71,
      "text": "Downs, Horn, Howe, Squire and White",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4791.71,
      "end": 4793.37,
      "text": "The album's going to be called Drama",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4793.37,
      "end": 4795.35,
      "text": "And the track you just heard was Into The Lens",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4795.35,
      "end": 4796.63,
      "text": "Now I've got one up on you",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4796.63,
      "end": 4800.85,
      "text": "Yesterday afternoon I was invited to the office of one Foxy Fowler",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4800.85,
      "end": 4801.79,
      "text": "As he's known in the business",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4801.79,
      "end": 4804.31,
      "text": "Who's the head of promotion for Atlantic Records, their record company",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4804.31,
      "end": 4806.47,
      "text": "and he played me the whole of the album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4806.47,
      "end": 4808.81,
      "text": "and I sat there thinking as a lot of people",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4808.81,
      "end": 4812.07,
      "text": "are going to be really sort of surprised",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4812.07,
      "end": 4813.87,
      "text": "because it works.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4814.23,
      "end": 4817.03,
      "text": "The Buggles and Yes conjoining really does work.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4817.29,
      "end": 4818.71,
      "text": "It's a masterpiece of an album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4818.71,
      "end": 4821.37,
      "text": "but you're the people who'll decide whether you like it or not.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4821.93,
      "end": 4823.77,
      "text": "In my estimation it'll go straight to number one.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4824.77,
      "end": 4826.17,
      "text": "As soon as we get other tracks in the album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4826.17,
      "end": 4827.15,
      "text": "I'll play them for you.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4827.61,
      "end": 4830.07,
      "text": "And may I say as well lots of luck to John Anderson",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4830.07,
      "end": 4831.81,
      "text": "in everything that he does from now on.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4846.35,
      "end": 4847.97,
      "text": "We've been humbled by our listeners.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4847.97,
      "end": 4854.51,
      "text": "we made a mistake rockers by acdc or rather rocker by acdc is on release in this country",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4854.51,
      "end": 4859.77,
      "text": "it's on the album dirty deeds done cheap just about the only album we didn't check",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4859.77,
      "end": 4870.57,
      "text": "can't win them all but we try from the album boston whatever happened to them and that was",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5220.0,
      "end": 5310.34,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5220.0,
      "end": 5310.34,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5310.34,
      "end": 5313.78,
      "text": "The Tigers of Pan Tang are bringing out their album very shortly,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5313.98,
      "end": 5315.34,
      "text": "and here's a couple of tracks from it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5315.78,
      "end": 5322.38,
      "text": "It features the Tigers of Pan Tang, two tracks from the album,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5865.25,
      "end": 5866.19,
      "text": "and it's coming out shortly.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5866.29,
      "end": 5869.29,
      "text": "The first one was Wildcats, and the second one was Slave to Freedom.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5869.51,
      "end": 5870.35,
      "text": "Sorry about the jump.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5870.89,
      "end": 5872.31,
      "text": "We were playing those off acetate,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5872.31,
      "end": 5875.51,
      "text": "and they're the worst things in the world to queue up on record turntables in studios.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5876.09,
      "end": 5878.49,
      "text": "Nonetheless, that was recorded, incidentally, when they were a four-piece.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5878.57,
      "end": 5882.21,
      "text": "Now they're a five-piece, and they incorporate another guitarist by the name of John Sykes,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5882.25,
      "end": 5884.27,
      "text": "and he's going to be making his debut with the band at Reading.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5884.71,
      "end": 5887.35,
      "text": "Right, back into the archives, way back to 1968.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5887.61,
      "end": 5890.73,
      "text": "This session features Mr. Jimmy Page, and it's by the Yardbirds.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5890.73,
      "end": 6089.38,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5890.73,
      "end": 6089.38,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6089.38,
      "end": 6094.18,
      "text": "In the carnets of ecstasy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6094.18,
      "end": 6096.58,
      "text": "Good night, sweet Josephine",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6096.58,
      "end": 6098.6,
      "text": "Listen, no one else quite like you",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6098.6,
      "end": 6102.64,
      "text": "If Josephine could, she'd give you her blood",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6102.64,
      "end": 6107.36,
      "text": "I know that she would, love to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6107.36,
      "end": 6127.98,
      "text": "Good night, sweet Josephine, we love you to destruction",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6127.98,
      "end": 6131.58,
      "text": "Whatever she does, the police will take no action",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6131.58,
      "end": 6136.38,
      "text": "They're all in love with Josephine",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6136.38,
      "end": 6140.58,
      "text": "It's right that Josephine should do just as she pleases",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6140.58,
      "end": 6144.86,
      "text": "And whether or not you like what she's got",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6144.86,
      "end": 6149.92,
      "text": "She's guaranteed not to blame you",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6149.92,
      "end": 6227.03,
      "text": "Yardbirds one more time with that super special Yardbirds sound",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6227.03,
      "end": 6229.25,
      "text": "And a song of their own called My Baby",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6229.25,
      "end": 6235.85,
      "text": "That was the last session they ever recorded for the BBC",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6390.03,
      "end": 6392.31,
      "text": "Way back in 1968, the Yardbirds",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6392.31,
      "end": 6395.95,
      "text": "The three tracks were Think About It, Good Night Sweet Josephine and My Baby",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6395.95,
      "end": 6398.45,
      "text": "And that was specially for all Yardbirds freaks",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6398.45,
      "end": 6402.25,
      "text": "who wrote in and demanded we play something by them out of the archives.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6402.77,
      "end": 6403.95,
      "text": "Here's Diamond Head.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6404.85,
      "end": 6410.85,
      "text": "From an album that's coming out shortly on Media Records,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6480.0,
      "end": 6755.36,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6480.0,
      "end": 6755.36,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6755.36,
      "end": 6758.38,
      "text": "it's by Diamond Head, and the track we played you there was called Am I Evil?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6758.54,
      "end": 6761.6,
      "text": "And I have a feeling we're going to be playing more from that album in the weeks that follow.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6762.02,
      "end": 6764.96,
      "text": "We're going to finish tonight with a track by Taurus, which is called Paper Chaser,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6765.0,
      "end": 6767.7,
      "text": "but just before I start to play it, let me tell you what Taurus are doing.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6767.7,
      "end": 6770.72,
      "text": "Gig-wise, on the 11th of August, the Old Kent Road at Redcar,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6771.04,
      "end": 6772.62,
      "text": "18th of August, London Music Machine,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6772.76,
      "end": 6774.74,
      "text": "19th and 20th of August at the London Marquee,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6774.74,
      "end": 6777.1,
      "text": "21st of August at the Bristol Granary Club",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6777.1,
      "end": 6779.1,
      "text": "23rd, Marshall Rooms in Stroud",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6779.1,
      "end": 6780.32,
      "text": "or Stroud",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6780.32,
      "end": 6782.52,
      "text": "24th of August, Effington Park Manor",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6782.52,
      "end": 6783.92,
      "text": "Stratford-upon-Avon",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6783.92,
      "end": 6787.64,
      "text": "and also they are at the moment in the process of getting a major record deal",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6787.64,
      "end": 6789.94,
      "text": "this track has been requested by a lot of people again",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6789.94,
      "end": 6791.84,
      "text": "it's Taurus and Paper Chaser",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6791.84,
      "end": 6799.04,
      "text": "that's another of the tracks you're going to find on Metal Explosion",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7157.14,
      "end": 7158.34,
      "text": "an LP coming out soon",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7158.34,
      "end": 7161.22,
      "text": "and that's it for this edition of the Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7161.22,
      "end": 7162.74,
      "text": "which I sincerely hope you enjoyed",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7162.74,
      "end": 7165.02,
      "text": "I'd like to know what you think about the new Yes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7165.02,
      "end": 7165.88,
      "text": "let me know in the letters",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7167.54,
      "end": 7168.94,
      "text": "Our engineer tonight was Malcolm.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7169.18,
      "end": 7170.6,
      "text": "Malcolm, we thank you for your help.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7172.29,
      "end": 7174.71,
      "text": "Our producer is Tony Wilson, who's been working since 7.30,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7174.77,
      "end": 7176.67,
      "text": "because he also produces Annie Nightingale at the moment.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7176.77,
      "end": 7178.35,
      "text": "He's walking around with stars in his eyes.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7178.45,
      "end": 7179.63,
      "text": "I'm going to ask him why.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7179.73,
      "end": 7180.81,
      "text": "Why, Wilson, why?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7181.98,
      "end": 7183.0,
      "text": "No, no answer.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7183.12,
      "end": 7183.74,
      "text": "Good night, everybody.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7184.82,
      "end": 7185.22,
      "text": "Gotcha.",
